From 923cb2eeb77a85db570401e9d622e00528580c1e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Christopher A. Williamson" <contact@chrisaw.io>
Date: Fri, 12 Jun 2026 10:35:44 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] securize: rework to property-based toggle with GSI
 fingerprint tracking

for release builds, replace the old securize script with a
property-based toggle gated by persist.sys.phh.securize and
/metadata/securize_disable.  on boot, rw-system.sh now detects
GSI image upgrades by comparing ro.system.build.fingerprint against
a persisted value and sets persist.pm.mock-upgrade so PMS correctly
runs post-upgrade steps even though securize overwrites the system
fingerprint with the vendor fingerprint.

the GSI fingerprint is persisted to /metadata/phh/gsi_fingerprint
(or /cache/phh/ on devices without a real /metadata partition) and
compared on each boot. when it differs from the previous value,
persist.pm.mock-upgrade is set to true.

securize no longer reboots the device on toggle -- the property
handler just creates or removes /metadata/securize_disable and the
actual prop spoofing takes effect on next boot via rw-system.sh and
phh-on-boot.sh.

other securize changes:
- remove phh-securize.sh from PRODUCT_COPY_FILES (now property-driven)
- add persist.sys.phh.securize property handler to phh-prop-handler.sh
- replace adb_secure handler with oem_unlock_allowed handler in vndk.rc
- add post-boot prop spoofing in phh-on-boot.sh for device integrity
- replace persist.sys.usb.config=adb with ro.adb.secure=0 in base.mk
---
